<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta name="generator" content="Helen">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../../../../javahelp.css">
    <title>Selecting several nodes with a rectangle</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img border="0" hspace="0" s7starttagpos="296" height="32" width="32" src=
      "../../../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp; Selecting several nodes with a
      rectangle
    </h1>
    <table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#000000" width="487">
      <col width="234">
      <col width="235">
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="477">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Use case: Selecting several nodes with a rectangle</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="477">
          <p align="justify">
             <b><font size="3">Comment:</font></b> <font size="3">If the user clicks on the
            background of a network and drag the cursor without releasing the mouse button, a
            rectangle of selection will be shown, which may enlarge or diminish according to the
            mouse cursor movements. Nodes (no links) that are within the rectangle will
            automatically be selected and those which are out, deselected. The steps are detailed
            in the following table.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="477">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Actor: User</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Normal course</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Alternative courses</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">1.When the type of editing is the selection of objects, the user
            presses with the left mouse button, without pressing any key, on the empty background
            of the network that is being edited.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">2.The use case <i>Deselecting all the visual elements</i> is executed
            so that nothing remains selected.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.The mouse cursor takes the standard shape of selection
            accuracy.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.In the position where it is been pressed with the mouse, a rectangle
            of size 0 drawn with broken line will appear.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td rowspan="2" width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.If the user moves the mouse cursor, the rectangle is resized. This
            rectangle will have a fixed vertex in the position where the user pressed and the
            opposite corner will be at the mouse cursor position.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.1.If the user does not move the mouse, the use case will remain in
            point 5.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.2.If the user releases the mouse button, the use case will go to
            point 8.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td rowspan="2" width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.If a node is no longer within the rectangle or none of them are
            longer outside, it goes back to point 5.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.1.If the focus of a node that was not selected is within this
            rectangle, it is selected by executing the use case <i>Selecting an additional
            node.</i></font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.2.If the focus of a node that was selected is outside this rectangle,
            it is deselected by executing the use case <i>Deselecting one single node.</i></font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">7.It goes back to point 5.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">8.The mouse cursor resumes its normal shape.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">9.The rectangle disappears and the nodes maintain their selection
            state.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
